# Part 3: agentgateway guardrails on kind, delivered by Flux. Run `just` to see the commands.

set quiet

# the commands of this project
[default, script('bash')]
help:
    cat <<'EOF'
    One artifact per component. Every component folder has its own justfile (it imports lib/workflow.just).
    Name the folder to run a recipe: `just platform/routes/build`.

      just <component>/build   render the folder (charts included), check it, write out/<component>/manifests.yaml
      just <component>/diff    the change against the artifact origin/main pins, that is what the cluster runs
                               (`just --set base <rev> <component>/diff` compares with another revision)
      just <component>/push    build, then push the artifact to the registry (host)
      just <component>/pin     write the pushed tag and digest into stack.yaml

      just clusters/kind/up | credentials | down   the kind cluster and the hand-over to Flux (host)
      just clusters/kind/delete-crds               remove the CRDs of the stack, explicitly (host)
      just tests/run                               the attack cases against the gateway

    Everything a component writes is in out/<component>/ (gitignored). What goes where: lib/workflow.just.
    EOF
